  "observations": [
    "Command-A selected all 10 modules. Command-U disconnected all 11 cables; video edges changed 9 to 0. Command-Z restored wiring and moving preview; Command-Shift-Z disconnected again; another undo restored.",
    "Command-E bypassed all module kinds. Bypassing Frame Delay removes the only causal edge; the feedback graph then reported three renderer errors per tick as expected. Undo stopped further error accumulation and restored preview. Adapter errors remained zero.",
    "Command-I reset selected modules: autosave confirmed default RVX parameters and preserved 11 cables. Core Audio reset closed its device, as expected for Rack initialization. Undo restored values, device and moving preview. This is logical device close/reopen, not physical unplug.",
    "Command-D duplicated modules without cables: 16 RVX nodes, 9 video edges. Undo then Command-Shift-D duplicated modules and cables: 16 RVX nodes, 18 video edges; both previews moved. That enlarged graph exceeded the frame budget (35.349 ms snapshot with accumulating misses). It was outside the agreed stress workload and was undone.",
    "Undo returned to eight RVX nodes and nine video edges, advancing output and zero adapter errors. Native window title no longer indicated unsaved changes. Other user Rack processes were left untouched."
  ],
